.0 (*)\n│   │   │   ├── tokio-util v0.7.18 (*)\n│   │   ├── oxide-tokio-rt v0.1.3 (*)\n│   │   ├── tokio v1.52.0 (*)\n│   ├── tokio v1.52.0 (*)\n│   ├── oxide-tokio-rt v0.1.3 (*)\n│   ├── tokio v1.52.0 (*)\n│   ├── tokio-postgres v0.7.16 (*)\n├── tokio-stream v0.1.18 (*)\n├── tokio-util v0.7.18 (*)\n```\n</details>\n\n**Platform**\n\n```console\neliza@hekate ~/Code/oxide/omicron $ uname -a\nLinux hekate 6.12.55 #1-NixOS SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu Oct 23 14:20:48 UTC 2025 x86_64 GNU/Linux\n```\n\n**Description**\n\nAfter updating our application ([oxidecomputer/omicron](https://github.com/oxidecomputer/omicron/)) to depend on Tokio v1.52.0, we noticed that some of our tests, which exercises code that makes use of `tokio::spawn_blocking` to perform file I/O, will now sometimes hang indefinitely. This is described in oxidecomputer/omicron#10272.\n\nSince we were updating from Tokio v1.50.0 to v1.52.0, I bisected which Tokio versions introduced the hang, and determined that the regression was introduced in https://github.com/oxidecomputer/omicron/issues/10277#issuecomment-4261943233. Knowing that our code was using `spawn_blocking`, and #7757 changed the internal implementation of `spawn_blocking` somewhat substantially, I tried patching our Tokio dependency to specific Tokio commits. I found that on the commit immediately prior to the one that merged #7757, commit 4c7d8b2a14de81ace4d8e61cfaeb8eca26f6f68c, the hang does not reproduce, but that on 1604bc335157be9a131e24cfde55cab3c90ebc92 (the commit that merged #7757) does reproduce the hang. See https://github.com/oxidecomputer/omicron/issues/10277#issuecomment-4262067619 for details. So, **I can say conclusively that 1604bc335157be9a131e24cfde55cab3c90ebc92 has caused at least some previously-fine programs to hang indefinitely.**\n\nI don't have a minimum reproducer yet, but will try to put one together. In the meantime, this is the test in which we noticed the hang: https://github.com/oxidecomputer/omicron/blob/0ef430324bbcc83b8fe3c733ce7629f2fd4faf93/sled-agent/src/artifact_store.rs#L1228-L1313",
