            "author": {
              "login": "hawkw"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I had hoped that it would be possible to move the sharded blocking queue from #7757 into an opt-in unstable `tokio::runtime::Builder` feature. However, unfortunately, this isn't super easy to put behind an opt-in toggle, as the sharded queue also requires changes to the code in `spawn_blocking` itself, making it harder to switch between the sharded queue and the previous `Mutex<VecDeque>` implementation. I had hoped we could just make the value of `NUM_SHARDS` , here:\nhttps://github.com/alex/tokio/blob/9de7950e59f8acea412600c2102ab592c419483a/tokio/src/runtime/blocking/sharded_queue.rs#L29-L32\ninto a variable, which gets set to either 1 or 16 based on the builder parameter. Sadly, testing this locally by patching Tokio to just always set `NUM_SHARDS = 1`, I can still reproduce the hang. Therefore, in the interest of just getting a fix back as soon as possible, I've opened #8057 to just revert #7757 for now, so that we can publish a patch release to fix the regression.",
